  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSR - UNDP Justice and Security Trust Fund II - SSR - UNDP Justice and Security Trust Fund</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SSR - UNDP Justice and Security Trust Fund II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till en UNDP administrerad multigivar trust fund som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka reformen av Liberias s&#xe4;kerhetssektor och r&#xe4;ttsv&#xe4;sende.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the UNDP administered Justice and Security Trust Fund with Liberia&apos;s security and justice sectors as beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Justice and Security Program (JSP) sought to support the efforts of the Government of Liberia (GoL), through the Ministry of Justice and the Judiciary in the consolidation of reforms aimed at strengthening justice and security institutions. The Justice and Security Trust Fund (JSTF) was established in December 2009 and became operational in 2010. As a component of the JSP, the JSTF was established to strengthen the operational and technical capacity of justice and security institutions to support overall security sector reform. The JSTF also suported the transition plan of UNMIL and government of Liberia. More specifically, JSTF has provided institutional support to five key justice and security institutions: a) The Liberia Immigration Services (LIS)&#xa0;b) The Bureau of Corrections and Rehabilitation (BCR) c) Liberia National Police (LNP); d) The Prosecution Department of the Ministry of Justice (MoJ) including the specialized SGBV Crimes Unit e) The Judiciary.

The JSTF has focused on supporting the following outcome areas:
Outcome 1: Enhanced Institutional Capacity Development and Professionalization of Justice and Security Institutions
Outcome 2: Improved infrastructure for Justice and Security institutions (LNP, BIN, Customs and DEA and Judiciary
Outcome 3: Justice and Security Instructions Capacities Strengthened to Protect Border Points, Monitor Security and Respond to Crimes
Outcome 4: Mechanisms for Effective prosecution of SGBV in Montserrado &amp; Hub 1 strengthened</narrative>
  </description>
